From: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
Subject: [PATCH] uqmi: add SoC-integrated modem, PDC, VOICE and roaming commands

- fix --set-data-format, which parsed its argument but never sent the
  request. It is required on modems without the WDA service, e.g.
  Qualcomm SoC-integrated modems using BAM-DMUX.
- add --bind-data-port to bind a WDS client to the SIO port of a data
  channel ("a2-mux-rmnet<0-7>" or a raw port number)
- add support for waiting on indications, used by requests whose result
  is delivered later as an indication, and UQMI_DEBUG=1 to dump all
  messages
- add the PDC commands (--pdc-list-configs, --pdc-get-selected-config,
  --pdc-load-config, --pdc-activate-config, --pdc-deactivate-config,
  --pdc-delete-config, --pdc-config-type)
- add the VOICE commands (--voice-dial, --voice-end-call,
  --voice-answer-call, --voice-get-all-call-info, --voice-burst-dtmf,
  --voice-start-dtmf, --voice-stop-dtmf, --voice-indications)
- add --get-network-roaming and --network-change-duration to the NAS
  commands
- use the shared SMS codec, frame, PDC, voice and WDS helpers of the
  common library
